campaigns.desc:
&lt;BODY&gt;&lt;P&gt;Set in 1965, Fail Safe is a prequel to "Northern Inferno" (1975) and "Red Tide" (1985).&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;A Soviet Yak-27 mysteriously crash-landed in the remote Svalbard Islands after a daring covert overflight of NATO bases in Greenland. Tensions have skyrocketed as NATO demands answers from the Soviet Union, but the Kremlin remains ominously silent. As the standoff intensifies, NATO has mobilized a formidable force to counter any emerging threats from the Soviets. Intelligence suggests the Soviets are scrambling to recover the aircraft wreckage, escalating the high-stakes race against time.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Do you have what it takes to stand up to Soviet Forces and avert Armageddon?&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

campaigns.end:
&lt;BODY&gt;&lt;P&gt;Following NATO strikes into the Soviet Union by NATO CVBGs, Soviet forces have now retaliated by hitting major population centres in Europe; this was followed by a relentless exchange of nuclear weapons on both sides. World War III is now fully underway as the Soviets rain nuclear weapons all over Europe. Bear and Bison bombers attacking the United Kingdom are stopped by the RAF, but cities and industrial areas on the eastern side of the UK are being destroyed by a firestorm caused by Soviet bombs and medium-range missiles fired from Golf-class submarines.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;President Johnson has ordered all American nuclear forces into action, utilizing the preliminary plans laid out in the National Security Council's NSC 162/2 directive. US B-52 bombers on the ground and in the air are launched towards their targets in the Soviet Union. Russian Bear and Bison bombers are heading in further swarms over the Canadian northern frontier.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The nuclear exchange has now spread throughout the known world with surviving NATO forces and WESTPAC units exchanging fire as far as China trying to counter the remaining Soviet threat. The world stands on the brink of extinction....&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;“Now I Am Become Death, the Destroyer of Worlds.”&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt;-The line, from the Hindu “The Bhagavad Gita”, Quoted by Robert Oppenheimer&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY style="FONT-SIZE: xx-small; FONT-FAMILY: Segoe UI; FONT-WEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;The Battle of the South China Sea was less decisive than either side had hoped. The series of embarrassments experienced by the PLAN that led to the battle permanently scarred the forces' reputation. For the Anti-China ASEAN coalition, despite defending their sovereignty, losses were high. The economic sanctions placed on these states by Beijing would cripple the regional economy and prolong Southeast Asian reliance on European and American markets. &lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;The true winners of the battle were in Washington. Shortly after the final engagements, an American-led peacekeeping task force descended on the region, preventing further escalation. Through backroom deals and covert support, the United States had successfully tangled its rival into a neo-colonial sideshow in the South China Sea. Little had changed in the region as the tides of war continued to ebb and flow.&lt;/FONT&gt; &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

campaigns.desc:
&lt;BODY&gt;Strike Tutorial&lt;/STRONG&gt; 
&lt;P&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This is a simple campaign comprising a series of simple tutorials that will take you from the most basic of air attacks to quite advanced methods of using stealth, jamming, SEAD and deception.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Created by Gunner98 aka Bart Gauvin.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

