&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;st1:country-region w:st="on"&gt;Brunei&lt;/st1:country-region&gt; has requested Military assistance from the &lt;st1:country-region w:st="on"&gt;United Kingdom&lt;/st1:country-region&gt;, &lt;st1:country-region w:st="on"&gt;Australia&lt;/st1:country-region&gt; and &lt;st1:country-region w:st="on"&gt;&lt;st1:place w:st="on"&gt;New Zealand&lt;/st1:place&gt;&lt;/st1:country-region&gt;.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;The United Kingdom Government has diverted a Bersama Lima Deployment (TU 544.01.02 and TU 544.01.03 from &lt;st1:country-region w:st="on"&gt;Singapore&lt;/st1:country-region&gt; to the &lt;st1:place w:st="on"&gt;South China Sea&lt;/st1:place&gt; in Response.TU 544.01.01 is already on station in the Brunei EEZ.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;Author and Scenario Designer&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="TEXT-DECORATION: none; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); TEXT-ALIGN: left; FONT: 400 12px Verdana; ORPHANS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(225,225,225); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: 100%; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT style="BACKGROUND-COLOR: #e1e1e1" face=Verdana&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT style="BACKGROUND-COLOR: #e1e1e1" face=Verdana&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY text=#dcdcdc bgColor=#2b2b2b scroll=auto&gt;&lt;FONT style="BACKGROUND-COLOR: #2b2b2b"&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto"&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Date/Time:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;2 January, 1997/ 05:00:00 Zulu&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Crimea&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt;&amp;nbsp;12 Hours&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt;&amp;nbsp;Russia&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT style="BACKGROUND-COLOR: #2b2b2b"&gt;Ever since the Crimean Peninsula was handed over to the Ukrainian SSR, it remained a sticking point until the 2014 Russian takeover. The possibility for a conflict over it or the rest of Ukraine in general hung over the region until it finally broke out that year.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT style="BACKGROUND-COLOR: #2b2b2b"&gt;This scenario features a far earlier conflict over the Crimean Peninsula, with the target being Belbek Airbase in Sevastapol. The Ukrainian arsenal has not deteroriated quite as much, they are far more willing to fight back politically, and Russia is fighting with its unreformed Soviet system. It will be a ferocious clash. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT style="BACKGROUND-COLOR: #2b2b2b"&gt;Scenario by Colin "Coiler12" Salt.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;[LOADDOC]Assets\Brother_Desc.html[/LOADDOC] 
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Miguel Molina&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; July 16th 2011 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Colombian / Venezuelan Border &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Colombia &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 3 days&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Historically, several low intensity conflicts occured between the republics of Colombia and Venezuela following their independence, chiefly due to territorial disputes. More recently tension has again grown, fuelled in no small part by personal disputes between the presidents of both countries.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Colombia claims that Venezuela is knowingly providing refuge to units of Colombian rebels engaged in an ongoing insurgency; conducting raids in Colombia and then crossing the border into Venezuela to seek safe haven and materiel support. Venezuela vehemently denies the allegations, and is threatening to sever all diplomatic relations with Colombia.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In the last month a new draft agreement between Colombia and the United States enabling the establishment of US bases on Colombian soil is perceived by the Venezuelan establishment as an open provocation. The seed for war is sown... &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;[LOADDOC]Assets\Canary_Desc.html[/LOADDOC] 
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Miguel Molina&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 12 October 2005&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Canary Islands / Moroccan Coast&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Spain &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 days, 6 hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The year 2005 was a tumultuous time in North Africa, as a succession of radical Islamist parties came to power; first in Algeria and then across Africa. By October the governments of Algeria, Egypt and Libya--along with the historically moderate governments of Tunisia and Morocco--would unite under the banner of the North African Islamic League; N.A.I.L.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Spain’s relationship with Morocco had deteriorated after the Perejil Island Crisis of 2002 and the failure of a referendum on the status of the Western Sahara. With the backing of the of fellow N.A.I.L. states Morocco began to press her claims to the Spanish held cities of Ceuta and Melilla. In response to the exacerbated tensions Spain increased her military garrison in the two cities. Just as tensions appeared to relax a secretly assembled N.A.I.L. amphibious force set sail and, overcoming local resistance, seized the Canary Islands.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Now, while the invasion is discussed in NATO and the UN, Spain mobilizes her military to retake the Islands.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;[LOADDOC]Assets/ChasingAphrodite_Desc.html[/LOADDOC] &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; September 30th 2019 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Mediterranean Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Greece &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 12 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Since the events of June 2018 when the Turkish offshore Drilling ship with the name Conqueror arrived in Attaleia port, the combined Greek-Cypriot Forces have been on High Alert. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;During the following months the turkish naval presence was limited around the Turkish shores. But after the political instability in Greece due to parliamentary elections (2019), the Turkish Navy has vastly expanded its activity in the sea area south of Cyprus, Eastern Med. A long period of tension between the three countries (Cyprus, Greece and Turkey) over the disputed offshore oil reserves of Cyprus (once a home the the mythical Goddess Aphrodite) seems to be reaching a flashpoint. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The successful negotiations between the Cypriot Goverment and ENI-TOTAL-NOBLE has opened new opportunities in exploiting the oil and natural gas reserves of Eastern Med. But the Turkish Goverment demanded its own share. With turkish Lira currency crumbling week by week and losing its value, Turkey needed immediate access to this valuable resource (oil), also known as Black Gold. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Almost a year has passed (September 2019) and the Turks made their move. They sailed across the Cyprus Exclusive Economic Zone and started drilling activities. The drilling ship "The Conqueror" was accompanied by a strong aero-nautical force! &lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;This action is an immense violation of Cyprus sovereignity.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Greek High Command requested an immediate response. &lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;You have 12 hours to accomplish your mission.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Your High Value Target is the drilling ship itself ! [1000 points] &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Patricio Ortiz&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; April 10th, 1986 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Approaches to Halifax, Canada &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Soviet Union &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 16 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;After recent, dramatic deteriorations in relations between the Warsaw Pact and NATO it appears war is imminent. Intelligence suggests that NATO forces are mobilising in American and Canadian harbours with the intention of putting to sea before the opening of hostilities. In order to mitigate the threat of American and Canadian forces to our operations in the Atlantic, the Politburó has elected to seize the inititative by launching pre-emptive disruption raids on NATO ports on the east coast of North America. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Charged with the command of a deadly Project 877 (NATO: Kilo) diesel submarine, you are tasked to covertly insert a special forces raid before laying sea mines in the approaches to the port of Halifax and engaging NATO shipping targets of opportunity.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;[LOADDOC]Assets\DownTown_Desc.html[/LOADDOC] 
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; December 1st 1967 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Gulf of Tonkin, North Vietnam &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; USN &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 1 Day&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Vietnam War began in November 1955, with US ground combat units deploying in 1965. The conflict escalated steadily, and following an attack on the U.S. Marine barracks at Pleiku in March 1965, the U.S. commenced Operation Flaming Dart, Operation Rolling Thunder and Operation Arc Light. These bombing campaigns would eventually last three years and expend more than a million tons of ordnance.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Navy strikes against North Vietnam were launched from the aircraft carriers of Task Force 77 stationed in the Gulf of Tonkin at Yankee Station. Although its official designation was Point Yankee, it was universally referred to as Yankee Station, located about 190 km due east of Dong Hoi.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The first missions flown from Yankee Station were reconnaissance missions over Laos conducted in 1964. During the two periods of sustained air strikes against North Vietnam, from March 1965 to October 1968 and from March 1972 to December 1972 there were usually three carriers on the line. The carriers conducted air operations for twelve hours on and twelve hours off to give 24-hour coverage, with two carriers operating during daylight hours and one carrier operating at night. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;A carrier would remain on the line for 30 to 35 days, and then have a recreation period for 6 to 8 days. A carrier deployment to the Western Pacific usually involved six periods on the line, launching 9000 to 13000 sorties, and lasting about 10 1/2 months. On rare occasions four carriers operated on Yankee Station, and for a short period of time during the Linebacker strikes at the end of May 1972, six carriers were on the line at Yankee station.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This scenario takes place in 1967 during Operation Rolling Thunder. You are put in command of the USS Ranger Strike Group, about to launch an early morning strike on North Vietnamese targets.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;[LOADDOC]Assets\Duelists_Desc.html[/LOADDOC] 
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Mike Mykytyn&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; September 3rd 1989 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Norwegian Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt; United Kingdom / USSR &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 Days&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The year is 1989 and the Soviet political strategy of bankrupting and breaking up the NATO alliance has been successful. America has pulled back into isolationism focusing on its domestic woes while Scandinavian and European nations rekindle pre-WW2 rivalries. The United Kingdom and West Germany now stand alone against the great Red threat. The Soviets move first by challenging Britain's mastery of the seas.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; July 21st 1977 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Nellis Training Range &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; USAF Students &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Established in 1954 and reinvigorated by lessons learned in Vietnam, the USAF Fighter Weapons School is the ultimate proving ground for the Air Force's best fighter pilots. In 1977 the curriculum centered around the F-4E Phantom multirole fighter which put students through a comprehensive syllabus of air and ground attack challenges.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The final section focused on Ground Attack Tactics and culminated in the GAT 5 &amp;amp; 6 exercises, run simultaneously with one section of aircraft striving for air to ground success and another for air superiority. Known by pilots as 'The World's Most Demanding Peacetime Mission', GAT 5 &amp;amp; 6 required eight students to attack an assigned target protected by staunch ground and air defenses. It was the fighter pilot's graduate thesis and the final obstacle on their path to returning home with the covetted 'Bullseye Patch'.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; July 21st 1977 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Nellis Training Range &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; USAF Students &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Established in 1954 and reinvigorated by lessons learned in Vietnam, the USAF Fighter Weapons School is the ultimate proving ground for the Air Force's best fighter pilots. In 1977 the curriculum centered around the F-4E Phantom multirole fighter which put students through a comprehensive syllabus of air and ground attack challenges.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The final section focused on Ground Attack Tactics and culminated in the GAT 5 &amp;amp; 6 exercises, run simultaneously with one section of aircraft striving for air to ground success and another for air superiority. Known by pilots as 'The World's Most Demanding Peacetime Mission', GAT 5 &amp;amp; 6 required eight students to attack an assigned target protected by staunch ground and air defenses. It was the fighter pilot's graduate thesis and the final obstacle on their path to returning home with the covetted 'Bullseye Patch'.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Ragnar Emsoy&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; October 17th 1957 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Norwegian Coastline, Finnmark area &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt; Norway, Soviet Union &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 6 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;MTBs are designed for high-speed night-time operations which enables them to get close enough to launch their torpedoes at enemy vessels. With next to no armour, the boats rely upon surprise, speed and maneuverability to avoid being hit by return gunfire.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This fast-paced scenario pits Norwegian MTBs against Soviet MTBs off the rocky Norwegian coastline. The scenario takes place before the advent of anti-ship missiles, and the player has to rely on guns and torpedoes to get the job done. In 1957 the Royal Norwegian Navy still operated a handfull WWII-era destroyers and these are integrated into the Norwegian forces for this encounter.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Ragnar Emsoy&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; October 17th 1973 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Norwegian Coastline, Finnmark area &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt; Norway, Soviet Union &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 6 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;MTBs are designed for high-speed night-time operations which enables them to get close enough to launch their torpedoes at enemy vessels. With next to no armour, the boats rely upon surprise, speed and maneuverability to avoid being hit by return gunfire.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This fast-paced scenario pits Norwegian MTBs against Soviet missile boats off the rocky Norwegian coastline. The scenario takes place as anti-ship missiles are entering wide-spread service, with Soviet SS-N-2 Styx-armed Osa boats of the 55th Pechengskaya Red Banner Missile Ship Brigade becoming operational 1961-1969, followed by Osa II boats 1965-1969. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;O&gt;Norway developed its own anti-ship missile, the IR-guided Penguin, which became the first anti-ship cruise missile developed in the western world. The missile was specially designed to operate in close proximity to land, being able to distinguish target ships from the countless small islands that dot the Norwegian coastline. The Penguin missile was first installed on a MTB in 1970 and entered service in 1972 aboard Snogg- and Storm-class boats.&lt;/O&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Ragnar Emsoy&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; October 17th 1986 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Norwegian Coastline, Finnmark area &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt; Norway, Soviet Union &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 6 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;MTBs are designed for high-speed night-time operations which enables them to get close enough to launch their torpedoes at enemy vessels. With next to no armour, the boats rely upon surprise, speed and maneuverability to avoid being hit by return gunfire.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This fast-paced scenario pits Norwegian MTBs against Soviet missile boats off the rocky Norwegian coastline. We're at the height of the Cold War, and both the Norwegian Navy and the Soviet Red Banner Northern Fleet are fielding large numbers of heavily armed missile boats. The nearly 20 Osa I and Osa II boats that entered service during the 1960s have been joined by eight Nanuchka I and Nanuchka III boats, packing deadly long-range SS-N-9 Siren anti-ship missiles and SA-N-4 Gecko SAMs.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;O&gt;The Norwegian Navy has 40 MTBs of the Hauk, Storm and Snogg-classes armed with combinations of Penguin missiles, anti-ship guns and anti-ship torpedoes. In addition, the Oslo-class FFGs have been refitted with Sea Sparrow SAMs and Penguin missiles.&lt;/O&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Ragnar Emsoy&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; October 17th 2016 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Norwegian Coastline, Finnmark area &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt; Norway, Russia &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 1 day&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This fast-paced scenario pits the latest Norwegian coastal stealth corvettes against Russian corvettes and missile boats off the rocky Norwegian coastline.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Cold War ended 25 years ago and no new missile boats have entered service with the Russian Northern Fleet for at least two decades. The mighty 55th Missile Ship Brigade on the Kola Peninsula was reduced in size to a Missile Ship Battalion and is now in poor shape. Only a handful Nanuchka III are seaworthy, armed with legacy SS-N-9 Siren anti-ship missiles and SA-N-4 Gecko SAMs.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Russian naval build-up that began around 2010 is showing results and the first Gremyashchy-class corvettes are entering service with the Northern Fleet in these days. The corvettes are armed with eight supersonic SS-N-26 Sapless anti-ship missiles and 16 SA-N-21c Grizzly SAMs, and embark a helicopter. However only two of these highly capable ships have entered service so far.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Norwegian Navy went through a dramatic force reduction after the fall of the Berlin Wall, with 40 MTBs of the Hauk, Storm and Snogg-classes being reduced to a token force of only eight operational Hauks by the mid-1990s. The last of the Hauks were retired in 2003, and were eventually replaced 2008-2011 by six extremely fast Skjold-class stealth boats of Surface Effect Ship (SES) design. The armament consists of a 76mm Super Rapido gun, eight long-range Naval Strike Missiles (NSM) in two flush-mounted pop-up launchers, and Mistral MANPADS for self-defence. The six boats, which were reclassified as coastal corvettes when the MTB service was disbanded, are rotated through service, with only four being operational at anyone time.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;[LOADDOC]Assets\GreenTide_Desc.html[/LOADDOC] 
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; David Perez, José Ramon García Paniagua &amp;amp; Miguel Molina&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; January 7th 2016 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Canary Islands &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Spain &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 4 Days&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;After discovering a large oil field east of the Canary Islands in 2011, Spanish oil consortium Orta commenced construction of five major oil platforms in the channel between the Canarys and Morocco. The proximity of the field to Morocco has generated controversy amongst the public of both Spain and Morocco, and caused significant tension between the two countries.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In the past 6 months Morocco has been suffering internal political strife, with an unpopular government facing challenges from a raft of opposition parties. A major corruption scandal erupted last month, which coincided with the completion of the platforms. Sensing an opportunity to divert attention away from internal issues and seize a valuable national resource, the government of Morocco has laid claim to the Orta field and associated platforms, declaring an 'exclusion zone' around the platforms and mobilising naval forces to the area.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Spanish government has just made an address to the United Nations declaring the Moroccan governments activities in relation to the Orta field illegal, and resolving to secure and protect the field and its associated platforms from foreign influence.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;[LOADDOC]Assets\IronHand_Desc.html[/LOADDOC] 
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Mike Mykytyn&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; May 27th 2014 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Nagorno-Karabakh &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Russia &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 3 Days&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Nagorno-Karabakh enclave remains one of the most contested pieces of real estate in what was once the Soviet Union. The conflict started in 1988 and escalated when the enclave declared its independence from Azerbaijan in January 1992, based on the desire of the ethnic Armenian population to gain autonomy from greater Azerbaijan. Armenia naturally sided with their ethnic brothers and contributed to a bloody conflict that ended with a Russian brokered ceasefire in 1994. Tensions since have continued to rise and fall driving a regional arms race, the occasional skirmish and putting Russia in a position where it once again may have to intervene.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Mike Mykytyn &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; September 9th 1985&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Persian Gulf&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Iraq&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 5 Hours &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Iran-Iraq conflict is one of the more interesting time periods for air warfare enthusiasts because the adversaries were so well armed and equally matched to face off against one another. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This small scenario places you in command of an Iraqi attack on Iranian oil facilities on Khark Island in 1985. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Patricio Ortiz&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; May 20th 1982 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Falkland Islands &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Argentina &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 36 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;During the Falklands war, the Argentine navy could deploy only two operational submarines: the &lt;I&gt;ARA San Luis&lt;/I&gt; (Type 209-1100) and &lt;I&gt;ARA Santa Fé&lt;/I&gt; (Balao-Guppy II). The other two submarines of the Argentine navy--&lt;I&gt;ARA Salta&lt;/I&gt; (Type 209-1100) and &lt;I&gt;ARA Santiago del Estero&lt;/I&gt; (Balao-Guppy II)--were respectively under routine maintenance and in the process of decommisioning. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The &lt;I&gt;Santa Fé&lt;/I&gt; deployed Amphibious Commando elements on April 2nd, and remained an active participant in the conflict until it was destroyed by a Sea Skua from a Royal Navy helicopter at Grytviken harbor on the island of Georgia. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Following the destruction of &lt;I&gt;Santa Fé&lt;/I&gt;, &lt;I&gt;San Luis&lt;/I&gt; was the only operational Argentine submarine remaining to confront the Royal Navy. &lt;I&gt;San Luis&lt;/I&gt; operated in several designated patrol areas, the most active of which were north of the islands, named Victoria (NW of Cape Dolphin) and María (NE of Cape Dolphin). &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;[LOADDOC]Assets/NorthPacificShootout_Desc.html[/LOADDOC] 
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Mike Mykytyn&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; September 9th 1989 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; North Pacific Ocean &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt; United States / Soviet Union &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 6 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The geography and positioning of Soviet and American forces in the North Pacific at the height of the Cold War always presented the danger of open confrontation. This was compounded by the not so subtle cat and mouse games played with military forces to keep the action at the negotiating table constantly in motion.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;[LOADDOC]Assets\BrassDrum_Desc.html[/LOADDOC] 
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Christopher Stoner&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; August 4th 2017 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Strait of Hormuz &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 1 Day&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Following the July 2017 attack on Gaza, the Islamic Republic of Iran demanded a UN censure of Israel as the 'unprovoked aggressor' in that crisis. Although the measure was enthusiastically supported by several member nations the proposal was swiftly quashed by the US UN Ambassador with a Security Council veto. Frustrated on the international stage, the Iranian President declared a blockade on the Strait of Hormuz until such time as the United States 'allowed the world to speak'. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;While only a few years before such an action would have been foolhardy, it would be unwise to discount Iran's ability to make good on its' threat today. In recent years the Americans' international prestige has suffered. In particular, progressively worsening relations with Russia have led to a state of brusque intolerance between the two nations. China has also been at odds with the US over their expansionism in East Asia and trade inequities. Both have worked to increase their influence with Iran, in particular by providing them a new generation of 'defensive armaments', despite the protests of a weakened United States.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The American President is not deterred from standing against the Iranian ultimatum. With only 1 carrier and an amphibious ready group in the region, with little else to support them, he orders a Freedom of Navigation operation through the Straits of Hormuz and authorizes pre-emptive action to guarantee its' success. It's a bold move that will demand the most from the limited forces available to the US Navy, where success will bolster the flagging prestige of the United States and failure means a massive loss of its' influence in the Middle East.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Mike Mykytyn&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; July 2nd 2014 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Pakistan / Arabian Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 Days&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;There is nothing more frightening to U.S. military planners than nuclear weapons falling into the wrong hands. Unfortunately the most likely places this could happen also present significant political and military challenges. That being so the US must be agile and decisive when using its military power to prevent what could be a horrifying opening to a Third World War. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In mid 2014 a Pakistani Army Brigadier with extremist ties has managed to convince his command to seize a Pakistani nuclear weapons site demanding that all US forces leave the region and Kashmiri territories be returned to their rightful owners or “God’s fury” will be unleashed upon Indian and US forces in the region. The United States cannot stand for this and must act. Due to current commitments the US does have significant assets in the region however they must be used well to succeed as Pakistan is a significant military power and an ally.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; August 27th 1972 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Gulf of Tonkin &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 Days&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Operation Linebacker was mainly carried out by air power. However naval forces were also deployed against important logistical areas and in support of ground troops. The Battle of Haiphong Harbor, or Operation Lion's Den, was one such engagement fought on 27th August, 1972. Four US Navy warships and a pair of naval attack aircraft launched a night raid against the port of Haiphong. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; March 1st 1968 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; South China Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; MACV &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt;&amp;nbsp;6 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Operation Market Time was the US Navy's effort to block the transportation of troops and supplies from North Vietnam to South Vietnam by sea. It was one of three Navy operations launched after the Tonkin Gulf Incident (the others being Operation Sea Dragon and Operation Sealords) in addition to naval gunfire support operations. Market Time ran for eight and a half years, day and night, in all kinds of weather.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;On 16 February 1965, a trawler was intercepted landing arms and ammunition at Vung Ro Bay. This was the first evidence of the North Vietnamese supply operation, and became known as the Vung Ro Bay Incident. The North Vietnamese trawlers were usually 100-foot long Chinese-built steel-hulled coastal freighters and could carry several tons of weapons and ammunition. The ships would sail out in the South China Sea, and under the cover of darkness, make a fast run to the South Vietnam coastline. Here, the ships would off-load their cargo to waiting North Vietnamese forces.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;To stop these potential infiltrations, Operation Market Time was set up as a coordinated effort using surface units along with maritime patrol aircraft for air surveillance and tracking. Aircraft types included SP-5 seaplanes, P-2 and SP-2 Neptunes and P-3 Orions. Many of these aircraft were armed with rockets or missiles, and were capable of sinking these boats themselves. Under normal conditions, suspect ships were detected by the aircraft and then challenged and engaged by surface units when they passed within South Vietnam’s 12-mile coastal boundary.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; December 4th 1971 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Indian West Coast &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; India &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 6 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;During the Indo-Pakistani conflict almost the entire Pakistan Navy fleet was based at Karachi Harbour, the headquarters of the Pakistani Navy. Karachi was also an important port for Pakistani maritime trade, critical for Pakistan’s economy. As such, the Karachi harbour was heavily defended against any air or naval strikes, and received the best defensive weapons in Pakistan's inventory in addition to being covered by two military air bases.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;On the second night of the Indo-Pakistani War of 1971, the Indian Navy launched a fast naval strike on the Pakistan Naval Headquarters at Karachi. Lacking strike range, four Indian Navy Vidyut-class (Osa I) missile boats were towed towards Karachi by a fleet tanker, escorted by two anti-submarine Arnala-class (Petya III) corvettes. Once in position south of the harbour, and supported by one of the Arnala-class ships, the three of the four missile boats began their attack.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; June 25th 1961 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Persian Gulf &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United Kingdom &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 Days&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The unpredictable Abdul Karim Qasim seized power in Iraq in 1958, un-stabilizing the region. In 1961, following Britain's withdrawal from Kuwait, Qasim unilaterally announced that Kuwait was to be considered Iraqi territory and would be incorporated into Iraq as their 19th Province. The British Government had given Kuwait assurances of military support in the event of an attack on their territory. So when the newly independent state called for protection, British air, sea and land forces were in place within days in a urgent military operation codenamed Operation Vantage. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

