&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;FONT color=black&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;United States&amp;nbsp;vs. &lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "st1" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:smarttags" /&gt;&lt;st1:country-region w:st="on"&gt;&lt;st1:place w:st="on"&gt;Iran&lt;/st1:place&gt;&lt;/st1:country-region&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;st1:country-region w:st="on"&gt;&lt;st1:place w:st="on"&gt;&lt;/st1:place&gt;&lt;/st1:country-region&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto"&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Date/Time:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;18th June 1988/ 03:30:00 Zulu&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Persian Gulf&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt;&amp;nbsp;8 Hours&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt;&amp;nbsp;United States&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;Situation&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;
&lt;DIV class=WordSection1&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="TEXT-ALIGN: justify; MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 98%"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 98%; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Book Antiqua"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;Operation Praying Mantis was the very appropriate name of an American retaliatory action against Iran in 1988. The subsequent battle turned into the largest that American naval forces had fought since World War II. It also marked the first surface-to-surface missile engagement in US Navy history, and the only occasion when a US ship has sunk a major surface combatant with missiles.&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="TEXT-ALIGN: justify; MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 98%"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 98%; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Book Antiqua"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="TEXT-ALIGN: justify; MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 98%"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 98%; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Book Antiqua"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;On April 13th warships of the Iranian National Guard laid a minefield in the main tanker passage, and the following day the USS Samuel B. Roberts&lt;I style="mso-bidi-font-style: normal"&gt;, &lt;/I&gt;struck one of these mines while on its&lt;I style="mso-bidi-font-style: normal"&gt; &lt;/I&gt;way to Bahrain. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: "Calibri",sans-serif; LINE-HEIGHT: 98%; mso-fareast-font-family: "Book Antiqua"; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA'&gt;&lt;BR style="PAGE-BREAK-BEFORE: always; mso-break-type: section-break" clear=all&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 98%; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Book Antiqua"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;Laying mines in international waters was clearly illegal and the US navy planned a retaliatory operation, codenamed "Praying Mantis".&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="TEXT-ALIGN: justify; MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 98%"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 98%; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Book Antiqua"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="TEXT-ALIGN: justify; MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 98%"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 98%; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Book Antiqua"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;The US plan was for a series of strikes to be made against Iranian oil platforms in the Gulf. As well as their drilling operations, all were known to be used as staging bases by the Iranian military. The intention was to expose to the Iranians just how vulnerable their vital oil installations were.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;Paul Bridge&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Author and Scenario Designer&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;[LOADDOC]Assets\Pyrpolitis_Desc.html[/LOADDOC] 
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Dimitris Dranidis&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; January 30th 2014 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Agean Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Greece &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 8 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Pyrpolitis (Firestarter) 1/14 was a COMAO exercise executed by the rapid-reaction elements of the Hellenic Air Force (HAF) in the early hours of Thursday, Jan 30 2014, as part of the the larger Astrapi (Lightning) 1/14 joint-force exercise. During the exercise, aircraft from multiple HAF airbases participated in assaulting a strong naval formation (and its air cover) off the island of Chios. This is a reproduction of the exercise scenario.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; September 7th 1965 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Indian West Coast &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Pakistan &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 8 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Indo-Pakistani War of 1965 broke out on 5th August when ca. 30 000 Pakistani soldiers crossed the Line of Control and took up position at various key areas within Kashmir. Indian forces responded, and crossed the cease fire line on 15th August. Soon, the armies and air forces of both nations were involved in intense fighting in the Punjab region and in Kashmir.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;To relieve pressure on the southern front, Pakistan launched Operation Dwarka, also known as Operation Somnath, on 7th September 1965. This was a naval operation that would attack the Indian coastal town of Dwarka, and would be the first use of Pakistan Navy in any of the Indo-Pakistan Wars.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The first of the two objectives was to destroy the radar station at Dwarka. Pakistani Naval intelligence believed it had a Huff/Duff (HF/DF - Height Finding / Direction Finding) beacon used to guide Indian bombers to their targets.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The other objective was to lure the Indian Navy out of the Mumbai Harbour and up the coast towards Dwarka so that the submarine PNS Ghazi could attack and sink the main units of the Indian Fleet. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;If successful, the operation would have a direct impact on Indian morale and it was hoped it could draw Indian Air Force units away from the north.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;[LOADDOC]Assets\Kismayo_Desc.html[/LOADDOC] 
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Christopher Stoner&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; May 13th 2013 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Kismayo, Somalia &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 5 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Reliable intelligence has determined that an al-Qaeda courier is bringing information coordinating further terrorist actions in sub-Saharan Africa to the leadership council of the Somali al-Shabaab faction. The National Command Authority has committed elements of the Kearsarge Amphibious Ready Group to act on this information if it turns out to be credible. Kearsarge and a lone escort, the Littoral Combat Ship USS Independence, have steamed ahead of the rest of their group in order to conduct this covert mission off the coast of the southern Somali city of Kismayo.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Their mission: to acquire and observe the courier in the chance that he will lead them to any al-Shabaab leadership elements and if so, to launch a direct action effort to capture them. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;[LOADDOC]Assets\Raven_Desc.html[/LOADDOC] 
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Mike Mykytyn&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 19 January 1976&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Gulf of Aden&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 5 Hours &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Following improved ties between the USSR and Somalia, the United States has stepped up air and naval patrols in the Gulf of Aden. Approximately one hour ago a Raven 21, a Navy EKA-3B aircraft from VAQ-130 Zappers, was on patrol over the Somalian coast before reporting lock-on from a surface-to-air missile battery. Contact was lost moments later and search-and-rescue beacons were activated shortly afterwards.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The President has given approval to land a small contingent of SEALs and Marines from the Tarawa ARG to locate and secure the crash site until a heli-borne rescue can be launched at dawn with support from the Oriskany carrier group. Tensions are high, and the operation will need to be skillfully conducted in order to avoid an escalation into confrontation between the United States and Soviet Union.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Soviet Union&amp;nbsp;vs. United States&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;/FONT&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Date/Time:&lt;/STRONG&gt; 17th May, 1979/ 06:00:00 Zulu&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Location:&lt;/STRONG&gt; South China Sea - Philippines&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Duration:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;1.5 Days&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;United States&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Following the downfall of the Marcos Government by Communist Rebels, Civil War has erupted in the Philippines.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;A small extreme faction supported by Vietnam, China and N. Korea&amp;nbsp;are violenty anti Western and have galvanised the Rebels into a well armed fighting force now known as the Philippines Comunist Force (PCF).&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Afew days ago the PCF attacked US Bases in the Philippines resulting in the deaths of 83 US Serviceman.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;President Carter has called a meeting of&amp;nbsp; the National Security Council who have now decided to take action to secure the safety of US Bases in the Philippines including stop and search policy to stop arms going to the PCF.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;CINCPAC has limited forces in the area in which mainly consists of Frigates and Destroyers.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;31st MAU and supporting assets have embarked in&amp;nbsp;Task Group 76.4&amp;nbsp;with supporting escorts.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The 31st MAU have been redeployed&amp;nbsp;from the Indian Ocean are now onroute through the South China Sea, the Group&amp;nbsp;is onroute to&amp;nbsp;Subic Bay to bolster the defences of the US Bases there.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Vietnam fully supports the Rebels actions in the Philippines and continues to supply arms and training to them.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Unknown to US Forces Soviet Intelligence has broken US Navy codes and know about the intended movement of US Units in the area.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Author and Scenario Designer&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; May 25th 1982 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; North-West of the Falkland Islands &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Argentina &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 6 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;On 25th May 1982, A-4B Skyhawks from Grupo 5 were given a mission specifically targeted at HMS Coventry and HMS Broadsword. The two ships had been on picket duty north-west of the Falkland Islands, acting as both early warning and the first layer of defence for the British carrier group. They had become quite a thorn in the side for the Argentine forces, and as a result, raids were scheduled against the ships.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Mike Mykytyn&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; January 20th 1991 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Persian Gulf &amp;amp; Iraq &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States Navy, United States Air Force &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 24 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Desert Storm was the most meticulously planned and decisive air campaign to date. War planners employed a massive arsenal designed to fight Warsaw Pact forces in Europe to systematically incapacitate and defeat one of the larger and more battle experienced armies in the world at the time. Target lists were large and complex and challenged planners to match the right platforms and weapons to the right targets while still moving the war forward with minimal loss. That is what this scenario is about.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This is a fictional air warfare scenario covering the 4th day of the air war that is playable from the United States Air Force (USAF) or United States Navy (USN) side. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Mike Mykytyn&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; June 25th 2015&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; South China Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt; United States / People's Republic of China &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 36 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;As China rises it has begun to press longstanding maritime claims with the hopes of rolling back potential adversaries farther from its shores, opening up Chinese industry to new opportunities and securing the sea lines of communication to the natural resources its booming industry requires. It is strategy borne on the notion that the PLAN vastly outclasses most nations in the region and that the United States will never risk war or economic disaster over a small maritime claim. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Scarborough Shoal or Huangyan Island is a small group of islands, reefs and rocks around 123 miles from Subic Bay. Sparsely populated and of marginal value to the fishing industry its ownership is contested by the Philippines and the People’s Republic of China. China has begun more recently sending Coast Guard vessels along with its fishing fleet to protect its interests. With the U.S. forces on the not so distant horizon the Philippine Navy may feel empowered to act.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; January 18th 2011 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Falkland Islands / Las Malvinas &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt; United Kingdom / Argentina &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 36 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Fighting an expensive land insurgency in southwest Asia has forced the UK Ministry of Defense to gut the Royal Navy and Royal Air Force faster than any likely adversary could ever hope to. The drawn out and unpopular conflict continues to stretch the MoD thin, while political machinations steadily erode the power projection capabilities of the Royal Navy.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;With internal strife brewing in Argentina, an old adversary sees an opportunity to better its position, renew a nationally important--and popular--claim and cement a win in the looming election. Will history repeat itself?&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; November 24th 1979 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Norwegian Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; NATO &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 3 Days &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The destroyer USS Farragut (DDG 37) has been rammed and sunk with heavy loss of life while shadowing the Soviet Kynda-class cruiser Admiral Golovko in the Mediterranean. In Washington, the Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff have laid blame for the incident squarely on Soviet shoulders, while the President has demanded a Soviet apology and appropriate reparations. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In turn the Soviet Politburo accuses the US Navy's 6th Fleet of dangerous violations of international maritime law and has labelled the incident as "a tragic but predictable outcome of reckless US imperialism". Both NATO and the Warsaw Pact have placed their naval forces on full alert amid escalating tensions. In the Norwegian Sea, a US Navy Amphibious Ready Group (ARG) has just off-loaded a battalion of US Marines in northern Norway as part of NATO's Ocean Venture summer manoeuvres. This ARG consists of the LPH Iwo Jima, LPD's Austin and Ogden and the single escort frigate Talbot. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Shortly after receiving news of the Mediterranean incident, Iwo Jima was strafed by two Su-17 Fitters operating out of bases on the Kola Peninsula. The Commander in Chief Atlantic Ocean (CINCLANT) has ordered the ARG to leave the Marines ashore and to steam southwards at all possible speed to a safe Norwegian port, while the multinational Standing Naval Force Atlantic (STANAVFORLANT) is tasked to protect the Iwo Jima ARG from further attack and secure the Norwegian Sea. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;[LOADDOC]Assets/SultansRevenge_Desc.html[/LOADDOC] 
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 2 January 2025&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Mediterranean Sea&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Greece&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 20 Hours &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The events during this scenario is a sequel to the fictional 2019 Aegean in Flames naval scenario&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;After a major defeat, the turkish navy took time to re-evaluate its position in the Aegean.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;With the Israel Presence near the Cyprus EEZ, we cannot outmatch the triple alliance of Egypt, Israel and Cyprus.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Thus our main target is the oil reserves in the Aegean Sea. The Greek Goverment isnt keen on negotiating and it tries to leave Turkey with empty hands.Supreme Military Council has authorized a pre-emptive strike that would destabilize Greece's defence capabilities. The shock and awe will prevent them from sully escalating a war with Turkey's Defence Forces.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;With the delivery of the Anadolu LHD (mini aircraft carrier) and the aqcuisition of the F35 B aircraft (one squadron), the turkish navy gained blue water capabilities&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Together with the parallel delivery of a squadron of F35As located at the Balikesir AFB, the combined Stealth aircraft fleet comprises of a potent Alpha strike force&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The goal of this scenario is to sneak in the Greek Integrated Air Defence System (IADS) and achieve devasting attacks against both military and political targets like the Greek Parliament, Pentagon, Hi-SAM batteries (S-300 PMU 1and Patriot PAC 3) and SSM Exocet Coastal defence (located in islands in the Northern Aegean).&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;With the Sultan's order, now it is time to turn the table and conduct an air strike at the heart of the Hellenic Armed Forces. This will greatly reduce and destabilize their defence capabilities which will in turn, force them to hastly sit on the negotiation's table for the Oil share in the Aegean Sea.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;Pakistan&amp;nbsp;vs. India&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 8pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto"&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Date/Time:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;3rd December, 1971/ 17:00:00 Zulu&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Indian Ocean&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt;&amp;nbsp;12 Hours&lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt;&amp;nbsp;Pakistan&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;Situation&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;FONT face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;On 3 December 1971, most of the Pakistan Navy ships were operational. BABUR and MUHAFIZ were at anchorage. DACCA was at Manora anchorage at Karachi. SHAHJAHAN, MUJAHID and MAHMOOD both Minesweepers were in Karachi harbour preparing for passage to East Pakistan. The only other operational destroyer in harbour was BADR.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;ALAMGIR was under repairs scheduled to be completed on 15 December, 1971 and TUGHRIL was under refit. Two gun boats SADAQAT and RAFAQAT, were at Karachi under the direct operational control of MHQ.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;KHAIBAR and TIPPU SULTAN were searching for MV Jhelum about 80 miles south-west of Karachi on a mission to escort her to Karachi. JAHANGIR was also on patrol about 60 miles south of Karachi. She had been tasked to assist KHAIBAR to locate MV Jhelum and was to resume patrol thereafter. ZULFIQAR was on the inner patrol 30 miles south of Karachi.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;At&amp;nbsp;the outbreak of hostilities, BADR and SHAHJAHAN were ordered to join FOFPAK at Gaddani. The minesweepers were sailed and tasked to carry out check sweeps outside the harbour and maintain a patrol. Within a few hours of the outbreak of war, all operational Pakistan Navy ships had put to sea and were on their war stations as planned: the surface fleet operating off the Makran coast and the submarines in their allocated areas off the Indian coast.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;Paul Bridge&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin"&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Author and Scenario Designer&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style='FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-font-family: "Times New Roman"; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-language: EN-GB'&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Mike Mykytyn&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; September 23rd, 1971 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Caribbean Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 Days&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In 1970 Secretary Kissinger informed President Nixon that U-2 intelligence flights had confirmed reports of construction of a Soviet submarine base that could support ballistic missile submarines in Cienfuegos, Cuba. The US administration was quick to respond to the Soviet test with a series of meetings to reaffirm the 1962 agreement not to base offensive nuclear weapons in Cuba. The Soviets backed down and work ceased on the Cienfuegos complex.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;It is now fall 1971 and the Nixon administration is focused on China, Vietnam and a coming election. Sensing weakness the Soviets decide to try their luck again.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; April 19th 1972 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; South China Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States Navy &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 6 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;During the Vietnam War, on 19th April 1972, United States Navy warships clashed with three North Vietnamese air force MiG-17Fs, a number of torpedo boats and shore artillery batteries. The US Navy ships had set out to stop North Vietnamese troops and supplies from reaching the battle front in Quang Tri Province from the sea. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Battle of Dong Hoi was the first time since the end of World War II that US Navy warships faced an air strike, and marked the end of daylight raids by the Navy. The warships were attacked by North Vietnamese MiG-17F's as they were shelling coastal targets around Dong Hoi. One of the aircraft, having failed to hit the target on two previous attack runs, scored a direct hit on USS Higbee with a 250kg bomb. The bomb destroyed the ship's 5-inch gun mount and injured four men. The MiG-17F was then shot down by a Terrier SAM fired from USS Sterrett. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;USS Oklahoma City received minor damage from shrapnel resulting from fire from North Vietnamese shore batteries. Several North Vietnamese torpedo boats engaged the Navy warships as they escorted the damaged USS Higbee out of the area, and two torpedo boats were sunk by fire from the Navy ships. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;According to some sources, USS Sterrett also shot down a SS-N-2 Styx missile launched by one of the North Vietnamese boats. The launching boat was being tracked in Continuous Boat Track (CBT) mode, and the SPG-55 immediately began tracking the missile when it was launched. Sterett quickly fired a salvo of two Terrier missiles that vanished into the overcast and exploded, and the contact disappeared from the radar screen. However, it has later been confirmed that no SS-N-2 missiles were deployed by North Vietnamese forces until 1974/75, and it is not known what the Terrier SAM may have hit. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Dimitris Dranidis&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; August 22nd 1987 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Greenland-Iceland-UK Gap &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Soviet Union &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 3 Days&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In accordance with the doctrine of "Maritime Strategy", the US Navy has surged a powerful carrier strike fleet deep into the Norwegian Sea to pin down Soviet naval forces, particularly their vulnerable strategic missile submarines. As expected, this fleet has already been subjected into repeated attacks by Soviet air, surface and subsurface assets. So far the battle of the North has no clear winner. Losses on both sides are heavy.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Further southwest, on the GIUK line, NATO's SOSUS arrays have suffered heavy attrition as a result of Spetsnaz sabotage as well as air and missile attacks on the control stations in Iceland and Scotland. The front door to the Atlantic shipping lanes has swung open.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;To plug the gap, NATO rallies all its nearby assets (including most of STANAVFORLANT) to form a mobile ASW group such as the world has yet to see. Task Force Horton, named after the architect of the Second Battle of the Atlantic, comprises of two ASW helicopter carriers and dozens of leading-edge ships, submarines and helicopters, supported by ASW aircraft flying from NATO land bases: All with the purpose of hunting down and killing any Soviet submarine transiting the Scotland-Iceland gate. TF Horton is NATO's mobile submarine-killing field.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Soviet naval High Command cannot ignore TF Horton; but neither can they do a whole lot about it. Until the battle of the Norwegian Sea declares a clear winner (or survivor, as it is), no major forces can be shifted to deal with this unprecedented threat. The most that the Soviet Navy can spare to throw at TF Horton are four front-line nuclear-powered submarines. To break out enough submarines into the Atlantic fast enough, NATO's block must be removed within 3 days. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Can this quartet make a difference?&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Paul Bridge&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; Decembet 9th 1971 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Indian Ocean &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt; India / Pakistan &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 1 Day &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;By late 1971 tensions between West Pakistan (today known as Pakistan) and East Pakistan (Bangladesh) were growing. An Indian intervention in Indian-influenced East Pakistan seemed increasingly likely, and on 21st November the Pakistan Navy deployed PNS Ghazi--an ex-US Navy Tench-class diesel-electric submarine--to the distant waters of the Bay of Bengal. Simultaneously the Pakistan Navy deployed PNS Hangor--a Daphné class diesel-electric submarine--to the coastal waters off the Indian Kathiawar coast. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;On the night of 2nd December 1971 a large formation of Indian Navy ships passed PNS Hangor at close range in waters off Bombay. The Indian task force included the cruiser INS Mysore, the flagship of the Indian fleet. Certain that this indicated a likely attack, the captain of PNS Hangor transmitted a warning of a possible attack by the Indian naval fleet on Pakistani forces stationed in Karachi. Indian naval intelligence intercepted these transmissions, and two ASW frigates of the 14th Squadron--INS Khukri and the INS Kirpan--were dispatched to deal with the submarine.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Ragnar Emsoy&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; July 10th 2019 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; South China Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/B&gt; India / China &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 10 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The China-India territory dispute is probably Asia's least understood conflict. The two pieces of territory, Aksai Chin and Arunachal Pradesh, are thinly populated high-altitude wastelands. The Sino-Indian War of 1962 was fought in this territory, and although China declared victory after capturing most of Arunachal Pradesh, the Chinese army voluntarily withdrew back to the McMahon Line by the end of the year. The real cause for the escalation into war remains a mystery to this day.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The territory claims along the 6530 km border re-emerged at regular intervals, resulting in major military conflicts. The 1962 war was followed by the 1967 Sino-Indian skirmish also known as the Chola incident, and then by the 1987 Sino-Indian skirmish. An agreement to resolve the dispute was concluded in 1996, but in 2006 China put forward claims that all of Arunachal Pradesh is Chinese territory. A Chinese military build-up in the region began soon thereafter, along with numerous incursion into the disputed area. In 2009, India began its own military build-up to counter that of the Chinese.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The military build-up was then followed by a calmer period in the early 2010s where both nations went to great lengths to demonstrate their mutual good will. Despite reignited diplomatic and economic ties, many hurdles were yet to be overcome. The border dispute went unresolved, with regular Chinese "muscle-flexing" military incursions into Indian territory. Additionally, China expressed concerns about Indian military and economic activities in the disputed South China Sea while India remained sceptical about China's strong military relations with Pakistan. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;As China slowly grew into a major global power the country expanded its naval presence in and around the Indian Ocean region. In February 2013 the Pakistani government transferred operational control of its strategically-located deep-sea port at Gwadar to China. Gwadar is situated on the Arabian Sea, less than 200 nautical miles from the Strait of Hormuz, and became the westernmost link in the line of China-friendly ports stretching from mainland China to the Persian Gulf, also known as China's ‘string of pearls’. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The increased Chinese naval presence had strategic implications that were deeply troubling for India. Indian analysts felt that China's expansion upset the delicate balance in the entire region and would allow China to control shipping at three crucial chokepoints – Bab el Mandeb, the Strait of Malacca, and the Strait of Hormuz. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;India, striving to be in the "big power league", began launching adventurist naval visits to China's back yard - the South China Sea. The exact purpose of these occasional military deployments remains unknown. The only thing they seem to have achieved is irritating China, which is paranoid of any other military presence in the area. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This hypothetical scenario assumes another dramatic collapse of relations between India and China takes place in mid-2019. India moves a strong naval force centred on the aircraft carrier Vikramaditya (Ex-Gorshkov) into the South China Sea. Worried about India's growing naval presence in such areas of strategic concern, China has decided to answer the Indian move which they view as nothing less than a challenge, and sends the aircraft carrier Liaoning (Ex-Varyag) to intercept. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Dimitris Dranidis&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; June 15th 1999 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Arctic Ice Cap &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 Days&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Since the early 1980s, the Soviet/Russian Navy has been using under-ice locations as patrol areas for its SSBN force, typically employing its most modern and ice-capable submarines such as the Typhoon &amp;amp; Delta-IV classes. Far away from NATO's traditional ASW surveillance areas, these areas offer additional challenges for effective strategic ASW since they are accessible only by submarines, rendering NATO's all-arms ASW strategy ineffective and (in the marginal areas) they severely degrade sonar performance because of the drift ice.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In this scenario, the Pristina airport crisis in the immediate aftermath of operation Allied Force has rapidly escalated. NATO forces have clashed with dug-in Russian troops in the airport, with high casualties on both sides. General Jackson's grim warning ("I'm not going to start the Third World War for you") has not been heeded and the situation is indeed careening towards a full-tilt strategic confrontation. As an ultimate warning, Washington decides to demonstrate to the Russian political leadership the vulnerability of its supposedly "secure" retaliatory strike force. Among other actions, this means attacking Russian SSBNs deep under the polar ice.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Original Concept By:&lt;/B&gt; Ragnar Emsoy&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; October 1st 1985 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Mediterranean &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Israel &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 13 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In response to IDF forces apprehending a known senior commander, PLO Force 17 operatives hijacked a small Israeli yacht and executed 3 Israeli citizens. Israel responds by conducting a surprise early morning air raid on PLO infrastructure in what is thought to be a safe haven, Tunisia.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 9 October 2017 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Arctic Ocean &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Russia &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 16 hours &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;As the Russian Federation re-asserts its role as a major world power following the collapse of communism, tensions have increased over several flashpoints in the Russian sphere of influence. Senior members of the Russian Defence Ministry wish to demonstrate that Russia retains and is improving its strategic submarine-launched nuclear missile capability.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;As part of a series of drills to improve readiness within the Russian Navy and to demonstrate capability to the world, a Delta IV SSBN is tasked to evade a capable force of the Northern fleet’s most modern vessels before delivering a simulated nuclear strike against an airfield on the Kamchatka peninsula.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 25 March 1987 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; West Atlantic &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Soviet Union &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 32 hours &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The United States enjoyed technical superiority in terms of sonar, signal processing and submarine quieting for the majority of the Cold War. In the mid-1980s however, the Soviet Union made massive leaps in quieting their submarines, with the newest Victor-III class submarines being comparable in stealth to the United States Sturgeon class. These dramatic advances were in no small part the result of the Walker spy ring, and the Toshiba-Kongsberg affair. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;After decades of being ‘one step behind’ in terms of operational freedom, in the spring of 1987 Admiral Chernavin initiated Operation Atrina, known afterwards in US naval intelligence circles as ‘The Great Soviet Sub Suckerpunch.’&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 28 August 1950 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Sea of Japan &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 days &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The UN intervention in Korea is going poorly. The Korean People’s Army (KPA) has pushed UN forces back to a pocket extending approximately 60nm from the port of Busan. The remnants of the Republic of Korea (RoK) Army and the US 8th Army are currently preparing to mount a desperate defense of this perimeter along the Nakdong River. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The speed and momentum of the KPA assault has exceeded all pre-war calculations; intelligence suspects that the KPA is receiving material assistance from the Soviet Union and People’s Republic of China. While the bulk of the US 7th Fleet prepares to mount a counter-attack at Seoul, the &lt;I&gt;USS Segundo&lt;/I&gt; is tasked with identifying Soviet shipping that may be assisting in the war effort.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 7 September 1978 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Adriatic Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 16 hours &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The arrival of &lt;I&gt;USS Preserver&lt;/I&gt; (ARS 8) in Tivat, Yugoslavia on the 8th of August 1978 marked the first time in history a United States Navy vessel had entered a Yugoslavian port for routine repairs, and was a significant step forward in US-Yugoslavia relations. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;NFSP-01--the first convoy carrying military materiel from the United States to Yugoslavia under president Carter's military aide programme--is approaching its destination port of Split and is due to arrive in 12 hours at 0900L. Meanwhile, the Soviet union has announced a 'Naval Quarantine' of the Adriatic and has publicly committed to preventing arms reaching Yugoslavia.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The &lt;I&gt;USS Memphis&lt;/I&gt;, operating with the support of the &lt;I&gt;USS John F Kennedy&lt;/I&gt; CVBG in the Mediterranean, is tasked with guiding NFSP-01 safely to its destination and avoiding a confrontation with the Soviet Union...&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 6 December 1985 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; East Atlantic &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Soviet Union &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 8 hours &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Yesterday NATO conducted a massive carrier borne strike against Soviet facilities in the Kola Peninsula and occupied Norway, severely damaging several airfields and logistic centres. In retaliation, Soviet Naval Aviation executed a multi-regiment missile strike on the NATO carrier group, sinking the carriers &lt;I&gt;USS John F Kennedy&lt;/I&gt; and &lt;I&gt;USS Dwight D Eisenhower&lt;/I&gt;. The remaining carriers &lt;I&gt;USS America&lt;/I&gt; and &lt;I&gt;USS Forrestal&lt;/I&gt; are headed south to replenish their magazines, with the presumed intent to return to the Norwegian Sea to assist in the sea control campaign.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;While the carrier strike group retreats to re-arm, the Red Banner North Fleet Submarine Division has one final surprise in store...&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 9 December 1985 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; East Atlantic &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Soviet Union &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 32 hours &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;After nearly two weeks of fighting, NATO force in Europe are beginning to falter. The front line is slowly but surely slipping west of the Rhine, with heavy losses on both sides. The surprise counter-attack by the Soviets in the Norwegian Sea has put extra pressure on NATO Sea Lines of Communication between mainland Europe and the United States.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In order to bolster their flagging defences, NATO is relying on a number of convoys from the United States carrying troops and materiel. While the Greenland-Iceland-UK submarine barriers are containing the bulk of Soviet submarine activity, a small group of Soviet submarines has managed to get into position off the west coast of France...&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 12 December 1985 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; West Atlantic &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Soviet Union &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 36 hours &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Third World War has raged for a week. Soviet ground forces have made massive gains in Europe, steam-rolling West Germany and pushing NATO back to the French border. Desperate fighting is taking place in Belgium and the Netherlands, while Norway is under attack in the north.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Due to the efforts of NATO anti-submarine forces, the Red Banner North Fleet submarine force has been largely contained within the eastern Atlantic where they are creating havoc with Allied shipping. Unbeknown to the NATO alliance, an elderly November class attack submarine has managed to approach the US East Coast undetected, and has just received orders to make her presence felt...&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 18 December 1985 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Cam Ranh Bay &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 12 hours &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The arrival of NATO reinforcements from the United States dramatically changed the situation in Europe, with the Soviet ground forces being pushed back beyond the East German border from their furthest points of advance in Eastern France and the Benelux. With neither side seeming likely to employ the use of nuclear weapons, peace negotiations are underway in Geneva. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Meanwhile in the Pacific Theatre, Vietnam and North Korea are under increasing pressure from the Soviet Union to open a second front to strengthen the bargaining position of the Warsaw Pact at the negotiating table. With the bulk of the Soviet Pacific fleet concentrated in the safety of the Okhotsk bastion, Naval Special Warfare Command in conjunction with the 7th Fleet has been tasked with sending a clear message to would-be adversaries in the Pacific. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 9 March 1992 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Indian Ocean &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 8 hours &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Emboldened by the military defeat of their neighbour and enemy Iraq, the Iranian Khamenei regime has become increasingly belligerent towards the Gulf states and United States. The recent acquisition of Russian SU-24 Fencer strike aircraft with anti-ship missiles has added weight to Ayatollah Khamenei's threats to close the Straits of Hormuz to foreign shipping.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;With an air strike considered to be too risky, President Bush has authorised a cruise-missile strike to remove the threat of the Iranian SU-24s...&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 14 April 1977 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Barents Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Royal Navy &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt;&amp;nbsp;1 day&lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Soviet Union's first aircraft carrier, the TAKR 075 &lt;I&gt;Kiev&lt;/I&gt;, entered service in early 1977 and caused a stir throughout NATO naval intelligence circles. Not only was the threat of Soviet carrier aviation a new and dangerous challenge for the West, but frustratingly little intelligence was available on the actual design and capability of the carrier itself.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;While on patrol in the Barents Sea monitoring the annual Red Banner Northern Fleet exercise Sever-77, &lt;I&gt;HMS Swiftsure&lt;/I&gt; of the Royal Navy was able to seize a rare opportunity to get up-close and personal with a Soviet capital ship and gain valuable photographic and acoustic intelligence...&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 28 May 1969 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Barents Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 days &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Intelligence reports indicate that the Soviet Air Defence Force (PVO) is testing a new fire control radar in a major air defence exercise centred around the Kola Peninsula. The Office of Naval Intelligence and National Security Agency are keen to analyse the electromagnetic emissions of this new radar in order to develop countermeasures.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;While returning from their North Pole deployment, &lt;I&gt;SSN 638 Whale&lt;/I&gt; is tasked with covertly recording the emissions from coastal air defences along the Soviet coastline.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 13 October 1998 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Okhotsk Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 days &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Following an attempted mutiny and hijacking of an Akula SSN in Severomorsk on 10th of September, there has been increasingly concerning indications of an impending coup by elements of the Russian Navy.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The chief concern is control of Russian strategic nuclear weapons, particularly within the submarine force. &lt;I&gt;SSN 21 Seawolf&lt;/I&gt; has been dispatched to the Okhotsk Sea to monitor Russian naval activity and provide a first-strike capability if the situation requires it.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 28 October 1998 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Pacific Ocean &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; Russia &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 2 days &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;During the removal of the failed Yeltsin regime earlier this month, &lt;I&gt;K-44 Ryazan&lt;/I&gt; disappeared in the sea of Okhotsk under suspicious circumstances. Recent imagery from remotely operated vehicles at the search site indicates that the &lt;I&gt;Ryazan&lt;/I&gt; was torpedoed.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Despite denials from the United States, our newly instated President Zyuganov realises that there is only one party who could be responsible for this unprovoked act of war. In response, President Zyuganov has ordered the most advanced submarine of the Russian Pacific Fleet to implement OPERATION TIGER SHARK to exact revenge on the United States. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;I&gt;"So let it be written, so let it be done.&lt;BR&gt;I'm sent here by the chosen one&lt;BR&gt;So let it be written, so let it be done&lt;BR&gt;To kill the first born pharaoh son.&lt;BR&gt;I'm creeping death..."&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/I&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Metallica - Creeping Death&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 26 May 2002 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Arabian Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; India &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 36 hours &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Tensions between India and Pakistan are at an all time high following an attack on the Indian Parliament in December of 2001. Both India and Pakistan have mobilised their forces, deploying hundreds of thousands of troops along the border. Mortar and artillery fire has been exchanged in the Kashmir region, and 2 days ago the Pakistani government commenced a series of nuclear tests.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;As part of the war plan, the &lt;I&gt;INS Shalki&lt;/I&gt; of the Indian Navy is tasked with deploying a MARCOS special operations team to the port of Karachi to conduct reconnaissance. The Pakistani forces are on high alert, and the entire region is on a thermonuclear hair-trigger... &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 17 July 1956 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Western Atlantic &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; RedFor &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 4 days &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The advent of nuclear propulsion with the introduction in service of the &lt;I&gt;USS Nautilus&lt;/I&gt; (SSN-571) was a watershed event for naval forces worldwide. Nuclear propulsion for the first time offered the capabilities that submarine operators had long waited for; true independence from the need to surface or come to periscope depth to replenish air, great underwater speed offering unprecedented tactical and operational freedom, and greatly enlarged available electrical power to support advanced command, sensor and weapon systems.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In addition to revolutionising submarine ops, the nuclear-powered attack submarine (SSN) also made existing ASW forces virtually obsolete overnight. The US and NATO navies had already been surprised once, by the impressive capabilities of the German Type-XXI "Elektroboot", and with the knowledge that the Soviet Navy would base its new submarine designs on it, had been forced during the first post-WW2 decade to undergo several expensive ASW modernization programs. At a stroke, the introduction of the SSN (and the acquired intelligence that the Soviets were already building their own first production run, the "November" class) threatened to make this investment all but useless. Nuclear-powered submarines were simply so much faster, so much more elusive, so much more capable that the hardware, tactics and operational concepts that had been perfected in the second battle of the Atlantic and further refined post-war would have to be re-examined from the ground up.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In order to fully develop tactics for its newest addition to the force, as well as train its existing ASW forces and discover ways to deal with the fast-approaching Soviet SSN threat, the US Navy performed a series of exercises between 1955-60, often with the participation of other NATO forces (such as Operation Strikeback in 1958 which involved over 200 warships, 650 aircraft and 75,000 personnel). This scenario represents a hypothetical ASW exercise off the eastern seaboard in the summer of 1956, in which you can choose to control either the &lt;I&gt;Nautilus&lt;/I&gt; or a top-line conventional fleet submarine. This is your chance to experience first-hand the nuclear-power revolution.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;B&gt;Date:&lt;/B&gt; 26 August 1984 &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Location:&lt;/B&gt; Barents Sea &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Playable Side:&lt;/B&gt; United States &lt;BR&gt;&lt;B&gt;Duration:&lt;/B&gt; 16 hours &lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Tensions between the United States and Soviet Union have reached heights not seen since the 1970's, with harsh rhetoric on from leaders on both sides, large scale military exercises (including the almost catastrophic Able Archer '83), and most recently the boycott of the 1984 Summer Olympics in Los Angeles. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Meanwhile, the US Navy has been successful in placing tapping devices on Soviet sub-sea communications cables in the Okhotsk and Barents seas. Following the Soviet discovery of the Okhotsk cable after a tip-off from a spy within the NSA, &lt;I&gt;USS Parche&lt;/I&gt; is dispatched to the Barents Sea to retrieve data from the Barents tap before it can be discovered by the Soviet Union. Tensions are high, and the crew of the &lt;I&gt;Parche&lt;/I&gt; are well aware that a compromise in their mission at this critical moment could spell disaster...&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;

